  "id": "DrugBank_DB01083 - MONDO_19182",
  "verbalization": "Orlistat, a lipase inhibitor, is indicated for obesity disorder and has been linked to monogenic obesity through its indirect pathway involving obesity disorder. The evidence suggests that Orlistat may exert a role in the pathogenesis of monogenic obesity by influencing metabolic processes associated with obesity. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Orlistat to monogenic obesity—through obesity disorder and its indications for rimonabant, cetilistat, and fenfluramine—indicates a potential mechanism where Orlistat could modulate metabolic pathways that contribute to obesity. These pathways are not directly linked to monogenic obesity, but their involvement in obesity disorder implies that Orlistat may have a role in the broader metabolic dysregulation seen in monogenic obesity. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Orlistat could be a candidate for repurposing in monogenic obesity, provided further mechanistic validation is conducted.",
